 why its sudden  departure from our screens is so  disappointing hosted by Jesus nice and  the kid marrow the series is an  outgrowth of their successful podcast  Bodega boys the Bronx natives have a  unique talk show style tackling topics  like sports pop culture and politics  with an irreverent wit and off the cuff  commentary their show originally aired  on the now defunct viceland before  moving to showtime in 2019. however in  2022 it was announced that the series  would not be continuing much to the  shock of dedicated fans the end of the  series came as a surprise to many though  marrow shared on the basic podcast in  August 2022 Jesus and I had discussed  pursuing separate interests over a year  prior to the show coming to an end and  that conversation solidified Us in  signing overall agreements that  recognized our intent to operate  independent of one another  reboots are not always successful but it  seemed like peacock's New Vision 4 Saved  by the Bell might be one of the lucky  ones the series which premiered in 2020  focused on a new generation of students  at Bayside High following the governor's  order to transfer low-income students to  the prestigious School the show also  brought back several characters from the  original including AC Slater played by  Mario Lopez Jesse Spano played by  Elizabeth Berkeley and Mark Paul  gossler's Zack Morris the show was  reviewed positively by critics with the  guardian writing the reboot depicts  social issues in a way that feels  authentic and in line with the show's  tone sadly Saved by the Bell was  canceled in May 2022 much to the  disappointment the fans were frustrated  by the abrupt ending per deadline for  instance it seemed as though Jesse and  Slater were about to enter into a  relationship at the end of season 2.  meanwhile showrunner Tracy wigfield told  TV line that she wanted to bring back  Leah Remini as Stacy for season three  something we'll sadly never get to see I  mean you were right  the on